WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
Pinocchio had always wanted to be on stage, but not like this.

2
00:00:04.841 --> 00:00:08.629
He was quickly sold to a circus to perform tricks.

3
00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:12.067
But the circus people were not kind.

4
00:00:12.068 --> 00:00:16.630
"Here you are, Donkey. Have some straw for dinner,"

5
00:00:16.631 --> 00:00:19.562
the trainer said, dumping it on the floor.

6
00:00:19.563 --> 00:00:21.822
Pinocchio tasted a bite of straw.

7
00:00:21.823 --> 00:00:24.914
It was dry and tasted like dirt.

8
00:00:24.915 --> 00:00:28.781
"Hee-haw," he complained, and spit it out.

9
00:00:28.782 --> 00:00:33.249
"What, you don’t like straw? Well, have some hay,"

10
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.921
the trainer said, dumping it on the floor.

11
00:00:35.922 --> 00:00:41.013
Pinocchio tasted a bite of hay, and it was as bad as the straw.

12
00:00:41.014 --> 00:00:45.768
"Hee-haw, hee-haw," Pinocchio complained.

13
00:00:45.769 --> 00:00:48.099
"Just you wait, little donkey.

14
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:52.535
You will be so hungry you will eat anything," said the trainer.

15
00:00:52.536 --> 00:00:55.909
And he whipped Pinocchio on the legs.

16
00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:59.829
Every day, the trainer would make Pinocchio practice.

17
00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:01.591
"Jump through this hoop.

18
00:01:01.592 --> 00:01:03.384
Walk on two legs.

19
00:01:03.385 --> 00:01:07.311
Dance the cha-cha. Balance a ball.

20
00:01:07.312 --> 00:01:11.121
Play dead," he would yell and snap his whip.

21
00:01:11.122 --> 00:01:15.826
If Pinocchio made a mistake, the trainer would whip him.

22
00:01:15.827 --> 00:01:20.795
One day, the trainer said, "Donkey, your first performance is tonight.

23
00:01:20.796 --> 00:01:24.003
If you do well, I will feed you grapes.

24
00:01:24.004 --> 00:01:29.183
If you make one mistake, I will feed you nothing."

25
00:01:29.184 --> 00:01:31.288
The circus tent filled with people.

26
00:01:31.289 --> 00:01:35.120
There were so many people that every seat was taken.

27
00:01:35.121 --> 00:01:40.957
"Ladies and Gentlemen, welcome to Vito’s Circus," said the circus owner.

28
00:01:40.958 --> 00:01:45.005
"I am Vito, and we have a special show tonight.

29
00:01:45.006 --> 00:01:49.539
This donkey has traveled all the way from Spain to entertain you.

30
00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:52.134
He has danced for queens and kings.

31
00:01:52.135 --> 00:01:54.632
He has jumped for dukes and lords.

32
00:01:54.633 --> 00:01:59.586
He has amazed children all over Europe."

33
00:01:59.587 --> 00:02:03.484
The crowd cheered and clapped, and Pinocchio did his tricks.

34
00:02:03.485 --> 00:02:05.650
First, he walked on two legs.

35
00:02:05.651 --> 00:02:07.501
Then, he balanced a ball.

36
00:02:07.502 --> 00:02:13.501
The crowd was smiling, and Pinocchio could see the happy children.

37
00:02:13.502 --> 00:02:15.829
Then, he danced the cha-cha.

38
00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:20.557
Pinocchio looked at the crowd again, and he noticed a woman with blue hair.

39
00:02:20.558 --> 00:02:24.546
Pinocchio jumped through the hoop and then ran out of the tent.

40
00:02:24.547 --> 00:02:29.521
The crowd cheered, and Pinocchio ran and ran.

41
00:02:29.522 --> 00:02:32.920
Pinocchio didn’t stop running until he got to the sea.

42
00:02:32.921 --> 00:02:36.869
There, by the water, stood the Blue Fairy!

43
00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:42.029
"Oh, Blue Fairy, was that you in the tent?" asked Pinocchio.

44
00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:45.368
"Yes, Pinocchio," she said.

45
00:02:45.369 --> 00:02:47.393
"Oh, I am so ashamed.

46
00:02:47.394 --> 00:02:50.655
I was foolish, and I was not a good boy.

47
00:02:50.656 --> 00:02:54.223
I am sorry. Can you help me?"

48
00:02:54.224 --> 00:02:56.825
"I know you are sorry, Pinocchio.

49
00:02:56.826 --> 00:02:59.752
But I cannot help you anymore.

50
00:02:59.753 --> 00:03:04.043
You must pay for your mistakes," she said sadly.

51
00:03:04.044 --> 00:03:07.347
"But, I don’t want to be a donkey forever.

52
00:03:07.348 --> 00:03:09.369
I want to be a boy again.

53
00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.119
I want to go to school.

54
00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.807
And I want to save Geppetto," he cried.

55
00:03:14.808 --> 00:03:17.391
"Perhaps you will do all those things.

56
00:03:17.392 --> 00:03:21.153
But first, you must undo your mistakes.

57
00:03:21.154 --> 00:03:24.966
How did you become a donkey?" she asked.

58
00:03:24.967 --> 00:03:29.149
"I was selfish and lazy," Pinocchio answered.

59
00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:36.686
"Yes, and if you do the opposite, you will return to being a wooden boy," she said, then disappeared.

60
00:03:36.687 --> 00:03:42.018
"The opposite of selfish and lazy is generous and hardworking.

61
00:03:42.019 --> 00:03:46.205
How can I be generous and hardworking?" he wondered.

62
00:03:46.206 --> 00:03:50.246
Then, Pinocchio got an idea.

